  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "The proof synchronizes two local essentially finite-presentation systems and a module presentation, forces both base and closed-fibre flatness at one finite Noetherian stage by killing finite Tor kernels, then uses faithful flatness to recover intermediate-ring flatness. The non-Noetherian two-level fibre criterion requires a genuinely substantial approximation/homological argument rather than a direct application of the Noetherian criterion.",
